### Task 2 — The OSI Model: An Overview
The Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model standardizes network communications across seven distinct layers.

| Layer # | Layer Name | Key Function / Protocol Data Unit (PDU) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **7** | Application | Network services interface for user applications (HTTP, FTP, DNS) |
| **6** | Presentation | Data formatting, encryption, and compression |
| **5** | Session | Tracks and manages sessions between host and target |
| **4** | Transport | End-to-end communication selection (TCP vs UDP); Data = **Segments** (TCP) / **Datagrams** (UDP) |
| **3** | Network | Logical addressing (IP Routing); Data = **Packets** |
| **2** | Data Link | Physical addressing (MAC), error checking; Data = **Frames** |
| **1** | Physical | Electrical/Light signals transmitting raw binary streams |

