### Task 3 — Encapsulation
As data moves down the OSI layers from Application to Physical, each layer wraps the data with its own header (and trailer at Layer 2). This process is **Encapsulation**. When data is received, the process reverses (**De-encapsulation**).

```text
[ Data ]                             -> Application/Presentation/Session
[ L4 Header | Data ]                 -> Segment / Datagram (Transport)
[ L3 Header | L4 Header | Data ]     -> Packet (Network)
[ L2 Header | L3 Header | L4 Header | Data | L2 Trailer ] -> Frame (Data Link)
